## Proof

**Setup.** Model the Möbius strip as the quotient
\[
E = ([0,1]\times[-1,1])/\sim,\qquad (0,t)\sim(1,-t),
\]
with projection $\pi(s,t)=\bar s\in B=[0,1]/(0\sim 1)\cong S^1$. The fiber over the basepoint $\gamma(0)=\bar 0=\bar 1$ is
\[
E_{\gamma(0)}=\{(0,t):t\in[-1,1]\}\cong[-1,1],
\]
using the $t$-coordinate on the $s=0$ side (with the understanding that $(0,t)\equiv(1,-t)$).

**Choice of Ehresmann connection.** The vertical bundle is $V=\ker d\pi=\operatorname{span}(\partial/\partial t)$. A sensible horizontal complement is
\[
H=\operatorname{span}\!\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial s}\right)\quad\text{at every point.}
\]
This is well-defined under the gluing: the identification $(0,t)\sim(1,-t)$ sends
\[
\tfrac{\partial}{\partial s}\Big|_{(0,t)}\longmapsto \tfrac{\partial}{\partial s}\Big|_{(1,-t)},\qquad
\tfrac{\partial}{\partial t}\Big|_{(0,t)}\longmapsto -\tfrac{\partial}{\partial t}\Big|_{(1,-t)}.
\]
Hence $H$ patches to a globally defined smooth distribution on $E$ with $TE=H\oplus V$, i.e. an Ehresmann connection. (Geometrically: "horizontal" = constant fiber coordinate, the natural flat connection on the strip before twisting.)

**Parallel transport / monodromy.** Let $\gamma(s)=\bar s$, $s\in[0,1]$. The horizontal lift of $\gamma$ starting at $(0,t_0)\in E_{\gamma(0)}$ is the integral curve of $\partial/\partial s$ with initial condition $t=t_0$:
\[
\widetilde\gamma(s)=(s,t_0),\qquad s\in[0,1].
\]
At $s=1$ this reaches $(1,t_0)$, which under the quotient is identified with $(0,-t_0)\in E_{\gamma(1)}=E_{\gamma(0)}$. Therefore the geometric monodromy is
\[
\boxed{\psi_\gamma:E_{\gamma(0)}\to E_{\gamma(0)},\qquad \psi_\gamma(t)=-t.}
\]

**Verification.** $\psi_\gamma(t)=-t$ is a smooth diffeomorphism of $[-1,1]$ (its own inverse), orientation-reversing, fixing the two boundary points $\pm1$ and the midpoint $0$. It is nontrivial, which is consistent with the Möbius strip being a **non-orientable** (hence nontrivial) interval bundle over $S^1$: a trivial bundle would have monodromy $\mathrm{id}$. The single twist encoded by $\psi_\gamma=-\mathrm{id}$ is exactly the half-turn that prevents a global section of the orientation line bundle, i.e. the obstruction to orientability.

### PROOF COMPLETE
